Improved: The step-100 tutorial program now assigns the
LAPACKSupport::symmetric property to the local Gram matrix and to the condensed
interior matrix, which are both symmetric positive definite. As a consequence,
LAPACKFullMatrix::invert() uses a Cholesky factorization instead of an LU
factorization to invert them.
<br>
(Bruno Blais, 2026/10/10)
